# What a run directory commits (README.md, "What is committed from a run directory"): run_meta.json,
# requests.log.jsonl, records/, queries.json, counts.json, merged.jsonl, screening_sheet.csv,
# prisma_counts.json, probes/. Raw response bodies are large, replayable from a run's own cache and
# partly non-redistributable (queries.json says per source whether the raw cache is published).
runs/*/raw/
# Smoke runs (make smoke) and the engineers' smoke directories are throwaway.
runs/smoke/
runs/smoke-*/
runs/smoke-*.log
runs/smoke-make.log
# Reviewer check runs (runs/review_<module>/, runs/review_<module>_b/ ...) are throwaway too.
runs/review_*
# Replay and twin checks (make replay-check, the literature/repository twin runs) are verification
# scratch: each is reproducible from the run it checks, and rr_replay_chk alone is 39 MB of records.
runs/rr_replay_chk/
runs/twin_*.log
# A relocated build (make ... MAIN_OUT=runs/<x>/manuscript/main.tex) leaves the same artefacts there.
runs/*/manuscript/*.aux
runs/*/manuscript/*.bbl
runs/*/manuscript/*.blg
runs/*/manuscript/*.fdb_latexmk
runs/*/manuscript/*.fls
runs/*/manuscript/*.log
runs/*/manuscript/*.out
runs/*/manuscript/*.toc
runs/*/manuscript/*.synctex.gz
runs/*/manuscript/build.log
runs/*/manuscript/main.pdf
runs/*/figures/*.png
# LaTeX build artefacts; main.tex and the tables are regenerated by sdr.manuscript and kept.
manuscript/*.aux
manuscript/*.bbl
manuscript/*.blg
manuscript/*.fdb_latexmk
manuscript/*.fls
manuscript/*.log
manuscript/*.out
manuscript/*.toc
manuscript/*.synctex.gz
manuscript/build.log
manuscript/main.pdf
# PNG twins of the figures (the PDF is the artefact)
figures/*.png
# Reviewer scratch outputs under tests/
tests/_out/
tests/*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
